    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u quickly summarize the actual steps a company has to follow when someone submits a \"right to be forgotten\" request under gdpr? just need the main points for a memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A company's process for handling a \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR involves several key steps, starting with the initial reception and verification of the request. You must first confirm the identity of the requester to ensure they are who they claim to be. If the request is valid, the company then needs to assess if any legal exemptions apply, like if the data is needed for legal compliance, and if so, they must document this decision thoroughly. If no exemptions apply, the company must proceed to erase the personal data across all systems within the required timeframe, which is generally one month. Finally, they must inform the data subject that the request has been fulfilled, or explain why it could not be fulfilled.",
