      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you miss some data, even if it's a forgotten scrap in a corner of a server, it absolutely can count as a violation. GDPR is very strict about the completeness of the erasure, and a single overlooked piece of personal data is a breach of the right to be forgotten. It's the data being *there* that matters, not whether you knew it was there. This is why maintaining an accurate data inventory, or a data map, is crucial before any request comes in.",
